WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:02.510
- There's a line in the documentary

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.630
that blew my mind so hard.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.360
When your parents are fighting

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.260
and you're growing up around that,

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.223
and your father says?

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.180
- "We fight because we love each other.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.690
This is what people who are in love do."

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.140
I was so young when I heard it,

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.290
and it stuck with me and it
clearly affected my mother.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.080
And I've spoken to my
father about this since,

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.950
and you know, in that moment,

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.980
maybe he was thinking he
was saying the right thing

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.640
to try to calm down a young child,

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.143
but you know, it's these
moments and these things.

00:00:33.438 --> 00:00:36.740
For me, the hardest part,
I always tell people,

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.520
as a parent is the things
you pass on to your children

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.238
that you don't mean to.

00:00:41.238 --> 00:00:44.230
And it's unavoidable,

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.860
it's just there's no perfect parent,

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:46.970
there's no perfect survivor,

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.160
there's no perfect person.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.080
You know, we all make mistakes,

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.950
and that's why I was
very proud of my parents

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.730
for putting themselves
out there like this.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:57.250
And you know, I know my
parents grew up in a time

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.120
where therapy was seen as
something to be ashamed of

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.490
and it meant you were crazy

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.750
and nobody talked about these feelings.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.410
It was sort of a different
approach to parenting, (chuckles)

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.243
which is just like,

00:01:09.243 --> 00:01:10.850
"Do as I say, not as I do," you know?

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.810
Like, "Don't speak
until you're spoken to,"

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.491
that kind of mentality.
- And they were young too.

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:15.330
- Exactly.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:19.140
- And that's what is so
incredible about the journey

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.140
that you do open up with
around this incredible subject

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:25.880
of what you went through

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.320
by including your family

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.490
and how you've grown up and
learned together as a unit.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.600
Now, then your mom and dad split up,

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.560
you guys go to Los Angeles,

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.640
your dad and your brother
stay in North Carolina,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:44.500
and you are 19 when you meet this person

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.770
who is so captivating.
- Mm-hmm.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.640
- So alluring.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.452
This man is giving you cameras.

00:01:50.452 --> 00:01:51.285
- [Evan] Mm-hmm.

00:01:51.285 --> 00:01:53.320
- You know, you think you're making art.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.660
- Yes.
- You're in a place

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.890
where you can do some substances,

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.460
feel free, take every,

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.250
feel that abandonment, that wildness.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.220
Was that a part of the entry point?

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.430
- Of course, yeah.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:11.100
You lure people in with this promise of

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.000
this is a better way, this is freedom,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.390
you can be who you really are,

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.360
we're gonna have fun,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.010
we're gonna do this a different way.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.480
And I think that's what drew me to Brian,

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.313
'cause I thought, wow,

00:02:21.313 --> 00:02:24.190
look what he's doing for young people

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:28.810
and the way he's
challenging the status quo

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:29.810
and social norms.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.860
And so that's what,

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.950
you know, I looked at him as a mentor,

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.630
as somebody-
- And it's sexy and it's hot.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.320
He's in front of all these crowds,

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.500
you buy and you drink the Kool-Aid.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.333
- You drink the Kool-Aid.

00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:44.570
And the analogy we often use

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:46.970
is the lobster slowly boiling in the pot.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.980
You don't just stick it
straight into the boiling water.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.090
You stick it in cold water,

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:53.580
and you're just slowly turning the heat up

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.852
until suddenly you're like,

00:02:54.852 --> 00:02:57.790
(chuckles) I'm sorry,
are you cooking me alive?

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.530
And that is sort of the analogy

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.283
for gaslighting and
grooming and brainwashing

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.730
in that you're lured

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.880
into this false sense
of security at first,

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.890
and this is why abusive
relationships can be so complicated

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.330
because so much of the
abuse is disguised as love

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.830
and that this is for your own good

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.460
or you don't know what
you're talking about.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.930
Somebody really takes control,

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.740
and as somebody that felt so inferior

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.960
to everybody my whole life

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.720
and just conditioned not to trust myself

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.380
and to trust the adults in the room.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.910
And then I dated somebody that
was 20 years older than me.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.750
He, to me, he's the adults in the room

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.980
and he probably knows better than me,

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.460
and so they made me trust them.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:41.590
You know, they were telling me
things that happened to them,

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:42.423
and then you feel like,

00:03:42.423 --> 00:03:43.890
oh wow, they've shared
something so intimate.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.730
I'm gonna share something so intimate.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.530
And then you start giving up your secrets,

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.250
your vulnerabilities.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.180
And it's the wolf in sheep's clothing.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.217
They're sitting there saying,

00:03:53.217 --> 00:03:54.530
"Yeah, no, absolutely."

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.620
But really they're mining information,

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:57.453
and they're going, okay,

00:03:57.453 --> 00:04:00.040
so that's what she's insecure about.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.930
Okay, she's got this relationship

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.070
that's broken down in her life,

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.100
I can attack that.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.020
And then, oh, okay, that's
what she's afraid of,

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.190
so I'll just feed into that.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.240
And we don't think this way,

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.470
and so we can't imagine
that somebody else would,

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:13.450
but people do.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.950
- When you are a kind, altruistic,

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:17.960
loving, caring person,

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.070
you don't believe that
other people are out

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:21.960
to get you.
- No.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.510
- Innocent.
- That's why you can't see it.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:24.800
- And you want the best

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.051
out of people.
- Yes.

00:04:26.051 --> 00:04:28.634
(bright music)

00:04:30.538 --> 00:04:32.621
♪ Oh, oh ♪

